WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:21.875
"Ratty! Please stop!" shouted Mole again.

2
00:00:21.876 --> 00:00:25.068
But Rat was far ahead.

3
00:00:25.069 --> 00:00:27.941
"It's my old home!" cried Mole.

4
00:00:27.942 --> 00:00:30.481
"I must go there!"

5
00:00:30.482 --> 00:00:33.670
Rat didn't turn back.

6
00:00:33.671 --> 00:00:37.616
"Hurry up, Mole," Rat called without looking.

7
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:41.270
"Oh, please come back!" yelled Mole.

8
00:00:41.271 --> 00:00:44.471
He stood in the road alone.

9
00:00:44.472 --> 00:00:47.813
Mole's home was nearby.

10
00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:51.096
"Should I go home?" he wondered.

11
00:00:51.097 --> 00:00:53.747
"Or should I go with my friend?"

12
00:00:53.748 --> 00:00:56.741
The choice made his heart ache.

13
00:00:56.742 --> 00:01:01.204
With a sigh, Mole ran after Rat.

14
00:01:01.205 --> 00:01:03.786
Finally Mole caught up.

15
00:01:03.787 --> 00:01:08.011
"Won't it be great to sit by the fire?" asked Rat.

16
00:01:08.012 --> 00:01:13.734
"Sure," said Mole, dragging his feet.

17
00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:17.350
Rat turned and looked at Mole.

18
00:01:17.351 --> 00:01:21.133
"Mole, you're tired. Sit down," said Rat.

19
00:01:21.134 --> 00:01:24.002
Mole sat on a fallen log.

20
00:01:24.003 --> 00:01:30.546
His lips trembled, and he burst into tears.

21
00:01:30.547 --> 00:01:34.672
"What is it, Mole?" asked Rat, surprised.

22
00:01:34.673 --> 00:01:40.756
"I know it's not cozy like your house," sobbed Mole.

23
00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.972
"Or grand like Toad Hall.

24
00:01:43.973 --> 00:01:47.945
But it was mine!"

25
00:01:47.946 --> 00:01:50.886
"What was yours?" asked Rat.

26
00:01:50.887 --> 00:01:57.470
"I went away and forgot all about it," cried Mole.

27
00:01:57.471 --> 00:02:01.270
"Then I smelled it again."

28
00:02:01.271 --> 00:02:04.546
"But what did you smell?" Rat asked.

29
00:02:04.547 --> 00:02:08.405
"My home!" sobbed Mole.

30
00:02:08.406 --> 00:02:11.465
"It was my old home!

31
00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:19.999
And you wouldn't turn back!"
